  "body": "**Summary**\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes issue #6525 where Next.js applications using `react-instantsearch-nextjs` would experience infinite loading when there's no connection to the search server during SSR.\r\n\r\nThe problem occurred because the `InitializePromise` component was waiting for search results using an event-based approach (`once('result')`), but when connection failures happened, these events were never emitted, causing the promise to never resolve. This resulted in:\r\n- **Server-side**: Large nested stack traces with `ECONNREFUSED` errors\r\n- **Client-side**: Infinite loading screens that never resolved\r\n\r\nThe fix refactors `InitializePromise` to use the more robust `waitForResults` helper function from `instantsearch.js/es/lib/server`, which properly handles errors and timeouts. The refactored implementation includes:\r\n\r\n1. **Proper error handling**: Catches and handles connection failures gracefully instead of hanging indefinitely\r\n2. **Better lifecycle management**: Uses React hooks (`useEffect`, `useRef`) for cleaner state management and proper cleanup\r\n3. **Abort signal support**: Allows cancellation of in-flight operations when components unmount\r\n4. **Maximum refetch attempts**: Limits dynamic widget refetches to prevent infinite loops (capped at 2 attempts)\r\n5. **Development warnings**: Provides helpful error messages in development mode when contexts are missing or operations fail\r\n\r\nThis ensures that Next.js error boundaries can properly catch search server connection failures, and the application doesn't hang indefinitely waiting for results that will never arrive.\r\n\r\n**Fixes**: #6525\r\n\r\n**Result**\r\n\r\nThe refactored `InitializePromise.ts` now:\r\n- ✅ Properly handles connection failures during SSR without hanging\r\n- ✅ Allows Next.js error boundaries to catch and display errors appropriately\r\n- ✅ Maintains backward compatibility with existing functionality\r\n- ✅ Includes proper cleanup and abort handling for React lifecycle\r\n- ✅ Provides better debugging output in development mode\r\n\r\nThe changes transform the component from a fire-and-forget promise-based approach to a properly managed React effect with comprehensive error handling and cleanup logic.",
  "changed_files": 1,
